A 47-year-old woman self-reported a palpable mass in the outer upper quadrant of the left breast that had been present for more than 2 years, with obvious size increase over the last half year. The patient had no previous medical history, no relevant family history, and no history of previous surgery.

A palpable mass was present in the outer upper quadrant of the left breast.

