triated patterns. No vascular or nerve invasion seen.', 'Immunohistochemistry': 'AR (moderate strength positive), E-Cadherin (+), Ki-67 (positive index about 40%), SOX10 (+), S100 (+), GCDFP-15 (+), PASD (+), PD-L1 (combined positive score = 3)'}}

A woman in her 60s presented with multiple dome-shaped, skin-colored asymptomatic papules located on the face and vulva. The lesions first appeared around 50 years of age and gradually increased to approximately 60 lesions. Medical history was significant for a meningioma. Family history was notable for a daughter with similar facial papules that had not undergone biopsy.

Multiple dome-shaped, skin-colored papules present on the central face and around the eyes, with similar papules noted on the vulva. No palmar or plantar pits were observed.

{'Histopathology': 'Eight lesions underwent biopsy, showing buds and cords of basaloid cells enclosing small cystic spaces. Clefting between tumor aggregates and the surrounding stroma was focally evident.', 'Imaging': 'Radiographic studies did not reveal any jaw cysts.', 'Genetic Testing': 'Whole-exome sequencing revealed:    - A conserved splice-site mutation in SUFU gene (c.757-2A>G) in all tumor and normal tissue samples    - Additional distinct deletions of the trans SUFU allele in all tumor samples    - No deletions present in the normal sample', 'Images': {'Title': 'Clinical and Histopathologic Features', 'Description': 'Shows numerous small, domed, skin-colored papules on the central face and around the eyes, close-up appearance of tumors, and photomicrographs of infundibulocystic lesions'}}

A white woman in her early 40s presented with generalized pruritus of 10-years' duration. She had no other medical history. She had been treated with topical corticosteroids with no control of the symptoms.

Physical examination revealed erythematous papules, some of them crusted, and some excoriations located over the trunk and upper extremities. In addition, some scales and fissures were seen on her lower lip, sparing the surrounding skin, as well as inner mouth and upper lip.

